# S5-07 canonical initramfs `norandmaps` sidecar diagnostic

Date: 2026-11-16

## Scope

Run the canonical Stage 4 initramfs in the existing automatic unique-nonce
N=2 `stage4a --user-mode --set-cpl0` profile with the opt-in Linux
`norandmaps` command-line parameter. Collect schema-v5 per-event page-fault
and CPL0 RDTSC sidecars to check whether the no-`norandmaps` run-to-run fault
and timing differences recur. This is a diagnostic, not counted acceptance
evidence. No comparator or normalization rules changed.

Series: `stage5-s5-07-canonical-norandmaps-n2-20261116-a`.
The runner source revision is `b6d5e7803c63f9b586776a1f5493440fd3526efb`.
Both runs used the same kernel, initramfs, CPU0 ACPI blob and manifest, 128 MiB
RAM, 3,000,000,000 retired-instruction budget, `nokaslr norandmaps`, and
distinct generated nonce values. The manifests identify the series as
`diagnostic_not_counted`; the sidecars have schema version 5.

## Results

Both guest scenarios passed, validated the exact nonce marker, and stopped
with `budget_exhausted` at `retired=2,999,999,998`. Each sidecar captured 33
delivered `#PF` events, all events present, and 22 CPL0 RDTSC sites with no
overflow or unattributed reads. The ordered `(RIP, error_code, CR2)` page-fault
signatures match between the two runs. This confirms that the differing CR2
in event 30 from the canonical no-`norandmaps` pair did not recur here; it does
not by itself establish ASLR as the cause of that earlier difference.

CPL0 RDTSC totals were 34,426,507 and 34,414,296 (delta −12,211). Six sites
differed; the largest contribution was −12,144 at RIP
`0xffffffff8271b34d`, previously resolved against this kernel's matching
debug ELF to `delay_tsc+0x4d`. The source of the changed loop iteration count
is not established. UART lengths were 23,513 and 23,893 bytes. The strict
automatic comparator returned `matches=false`, with unexplained differences
in `machine_observations` and `ordered_uart_bytes` after nonce normalization.
The UART difference begins in early boot output. Equal page-fault signatures
therefore do not make this pair deterministic or acceptance-clean. S5-07
remains blocked/unaccepted; no observed variation is classified as benign.

